Add missing translations

Several user-visible texts were hard-coded in English, so they could not
be translated. Move them to string resources:

- "Internal notifications" system notification channel name (existing
  channels are renamed to the current language)
- New contact sheet: phone number status under the number field
- Story privacy: dialogs shown when adding a group with non-contacts
  (plural forms; Cancel reuses the existing key)
- Forward options: Premium notice for hiding the sender name
- Story menu: "Wait until current upload is complete"
- "Unsupported content" toast when sharing into the app
- Location picker footer: "Powered by"
- Settings: "Experimental" section header

Show Ban, not Unban, for non-subscribers in channel Direct Messages

The monoforum topic menu treated any user who is not a channel member
as banned, so users who never subscribed got "Unban User From Channel"
and tapping it sent an empty editBanned. Use the participant's banned
rights instead and only offer Unban to kicked users.

Also fix the bundled UnbanUserMonoforum string, which read "Ban".

Don't crash adaptive dialogs when the theme has no window animations

AlertDialogDecor reads windowEnterAnimation/windowExitAnimation from
the dialog theme's windowAnimationStyle, which comes from the
platform's Theme.Dialog, and falls back to -1 when they are missing.
The id was passed to AnimationUtils.loadAnimation() unchecked, so on
ROMs whose dialog animation style leaves them unset, opening an
adaptive dialog (Create Link in the chat input, quick reply and
business link rename, fact check) crashed with
Resources$NotFoundException: Resource ID #0xffffffff.

Skip the missing animation and fade the dialog content together with
the dim instead. Dismissal still goes through the dim animator, so the
view is removed and the dismiss listener runs as before.

Fix playback speed icon lagging one step behind in release builds

SpeedIconDrawable passed an anonymous Drawable.Callback to its text
drawable and kept it only in a private field. Drawable.setCallback()
holds the callback through a WeakReference, and R8 removes the field
because it is never read outside the constructor, so after the first
GC the text drawable can no longer request redraws. The speed text
then only refreshed when something else redrew the button, which
happens at the start of the next change, so the icon showed the
previous speed while the toast showed the new one.

Make SpeedIconDrawable itself the callback: the view holding the
icon references it strongly.

Keep full resolution when editing motion photos

Drawing on, cropping or filtering a motion photo built the edited
image from the still decoded at thumbnail size (512px). That image is
sent as the photo when the motion is off, and as the still of the
motion photo when it is on, so both were sent at 512px or less. Decode
the still at the regular photo size instead.

Also stop drawing a live-off motion photo a second time without the
crop transform in the media editor, which left the unrotated frame
visible behind the preview after a 90-degree crop rotation. The
profile photo editor keeps its existing drawing.

