update to 13.1.0 (7229)

PhotoViewer: let fullscreen video use the hidden navigation bar area

In landscape the viewer hides the navigation bar together with its
controls, but the bottom inset was read ignoring visibility, so the
bar's height stayed reserved and the video was fitted above an empty
black band. Take the bottom inset from the visible insets, as before
12.9, so the video fills the screen while the bar is hidden and moves
above it when the controls (and the bar) come back.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/65941

Remove detached views from ChatBackgroundDrawable

onDetachedFromWindow() only removed the view when it was not in the
list, so a view was never removed. Every view that showed a chat
background stayed referenced by the drawable, together with its whole
chat view tree, and the image receiver was never detached.

This shows up when a chat with a custom background is rebuilt, e.g.
when a foldable is folded or unfolded: each rebuild kept the previous
ChatActivity view tree alive.

Don't count removed chat photos in the profile gallery

For groups and channels the photo history comes from messages.search with
inputMessagesFilterChatPhotos. The results also include
messageActionChatDeletePhoto service messages, which carry no photo and are
included in the returned count. They were skipped but still counted, so
the gallery made a page for each one. Those pages never load and show as
black or loading images.

Skip any result without a real photo and subtract it from the count. Only
subtract when one response holds the whole history: with several pages,
each would subtract only its own skipped results, the totals would differ
between pages and onLoaded() would rebuild the list, dropping photos that
were already loaded.

Allow replying to protected messages from the message menu

Tapping a message sent with protect_content (or any message with the
noforwards flag) and choosing "Reply" did nothing. The OPTION_REPLY
handler in ChatActivity.processSelectedOption() returned early for
every noforwards message, while swipe-to-reply and the Reply button in
the selection action bar already replied to the same messages.

The check was meant for the "reply in another chat" flow, taken when
the user cannot send messages in the current chat: quoting a protected
message elsewhere would leak its content. Move the noforwards check
into that branch so the in-chat reply opens the reply panel again.

Protected messages still cannot be replied to in another chat: the
menu does not offer Reply in channels the user cannot post to, the
handler still returns in that branch, and the reply options sheet
keeps hiding "Reply to another chat" for noforwards messages.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/65830

Hide Save in message selection for protected messages

When messages are selected, the action bar shows "Save to Music" /
"Save to Downloads" for music and documents. Whether a selected message
counts as saveable was decided by isPeerNoForwards() alone, i.e. only the
chat-wide restriction. The per-message noforwards flag, which is what a
bot's protect_content sets, was ignored, so a protected audio or document
received from a bot could be long-pressed and saved to the device. Photos
and videos were not affected because the selection bar never offers to
save them, and the single-message menu already checks both flags.

Saveability is now decided by canSaveSelectedMessage(), which checks the
chat-wide restriction, the message's own noforwards flag and the existing
view-once exclusions. Selecting and deselecting a message both use it;
previously the deselect path skipped the view-once checks, so the save
counters could get out of sync.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/66929

Popup notifications: tint the close button so it's visible

The popup's action bar never set an items color, so the X back button
was tinted with color 0 (fully transparent). It was still tappable but
invisible, leaving users with no visible way to dismiss the popup.

