Fix sending multiple files shared from other apps or picked via the system picker

Two related problems when sending several documents at once:

- ACTION_SEND_MULTIPLE resolved each shared content:// uri to a raw file
  path via AndroidUtilities.getPath() and uploaded from that path. Under
  scoped storage Telegram usually can't open such paths (e.g. files in
  Download/ shared from a file manager), so every upload failed with EACCES
  and the grouped message got stuck with a red error mark. With scoped
  storage the shared files are now copied into the cache with
  MediaController.copyFileToCache(), exactly as the single-file ACTION_SEND
  path already does.

- Files picked in the system document picker (attach > File > Internal
  Storage, requestCode 21) were sent one by one through sendUriAsDocument(),
  so each ended up as a separate message instead of an album. All picked
  files are now passed to a single prepareSendingDocuments() call, which
  groups them like other multi-document sends. When editing a message's
  media, the previous behavior is kept: the first file replaces the media
  and the others are sent as new messages.

Since the picker now groups its files, also fix prepareSendingDocuments()
for a group whose closing file fails (empty file, too large, copy error):
the group was never marked final, so the files already queued in it were
uploaded but never sent. The group is now closed with the queued files.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/66155

Bot forums: read updateMessageID before processUpdates when creating a topic

Since 13.0.0, MessagesController.processUpdates() removes TL_updateMessageID
entries from updates.updates before handling them. BotForumHelper called
processUpdates() on the messages.createForumTopic result first and only then
looked for TL_updateMessageID, so it never found it and completed with
topicId = -1. The message typed or forwarded into "New Thread" was then sent
with reply_to_msg_id / top_msg_id = -1 and landed outside the newly created
topic, which stayed empty, and the bot received it with no message_thread_id.

Look up TL_updateMessageID before calling processUpdates(), as
TopicCreateFragment already does for group forums, and match it on the
request's random_id. If no TL_updateMessageID matches, fall back to the
topic-create service message for this bot in the same response.

When topic creation fails, send the message as is instead of binding it
(and its local copy) to topic -1. The guard is the same one proposed in
DrKLO/Telegram#2179. The resent request is remembered so the interceptor
lets it through; otherwise it would try to create a topic again on every
resend, in an endless loop.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/66439

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Respect protected content for photos in rich text messages

Photos inside a rich text message are opened through
ChatActivity.openArticlePhoto(), which uses PhotoViewer's page-block
mode (originally built for Instant View). That entry point passes no
MessageObject and dialogId 0, so the no-forwards check in page-block
mode (isPeerNoForwards(currentDialogId)) always passed: "Save to
Gallery", "Open in" and "Save GIF" stayed available and FLAG_SECURE
was never set, even in chats with protected content or private chats
with Disable Sharing on.

Resolve protection from the adapter's parent MessageObject (peer
no-forwards, per-message noforwards, revealed paid media) and use it
to compute allowShare, hide the Save to Gallery button, guard the save
action, and apply FLAG_SECURE. Instant View articles, whose parent is
the page itself, are unaffected.

Also reset the "Stop downloading" item in onPhotoShow() together with
the other menu items. It kept its initial VISIBLE state on the first
open, so checkHideMenuItem() left the "more" button visible; with
"Save to Gallery" hidden this showed an empty popup. checkProgress()
still shows the item when the media is actually loading.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/64694

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Hide Copy in text selection when Disable Sharing is on in private chats

ChatActivity's text-selection canCopy() only honoured the peer-level
no-forwards flag for groups/channels (dialogId < 0). The private-chat
"Disable Sharing" setting lives on UserFull (noforwards_my_enabled /
noforwards_peer_enabled), so long-pressing a message in such a chat
still offered Copy and Select All for the selected text.

Use ChatActivity.isPeerNoForwards(), which covers both chats and users
and is already used by the message context menu, limited to cloud
chats so secret chats behave exactly as before. Also guard
TextSelectionHelper.copyText() with canCopy() as a defensive check.

Fixes https://bugs.telegram.org/c/66665

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Show EmailNotAllowed for EMAIL_NOT_ALLOWED on email code and 2FA screens

The email login code screen fell through to the generic "An error
occurred." alert with the raw EMAIL_NOT_ALLOWED error, while the email
setup screen already shows the localized EmailNotAllowed string for the
same error. The two-step verification recovery email screen showed the
raw error code as the alert message.

